Design a module for data compression and decompression. The module takes an 8-bit input data signal and compresses it into a 4-bit output by applying specific logic operations that combine groups of bits. Specifically, it generates the compressed signals by negating the AND results of particular combinations of input bits. Conversely, the module can also decompress the 4-bit output back into the original 8-bit input through a defined logic recovery process, effectively reversing the compression operations by negating the corresponding compressed signals to restore the original bit values.
